-- mlr2: this part's cases seat text, unchanged (merged by concatenation)
-- ============================================================
-- CASES for the seat layer (mlr2-seat.l4).  Each assertion asks one seat question with plain inputs and states the answer the
-- Regulations give, written by hand from the text beside the question in mlr2-seat.l4 (and the rulings in NOTES.md), not copied from the output.
-- The plain inputs are, in the order the question takes them, the comments above each group.

-- Each line: <question number from the seat file> | <plain arguments> | <expected value>, written by hand from the text.
-- A heading line starts with ##.  Comments start with #.  The name of the question is looked up from the seat file by number.

