-- ============================================================
-- mlr4: this part's cases seat text, unchanged (merged by concatenation)
-- ============================================================
-- CASES for the seat layer (mlr4-seat.l4): a business that is a relevant person, and its compliance officer.
-- Each case states the facts that person would state and the answer the Regulations give.  Every expected
-- value was decided by reading the provision, not by running the code.  @Y, @N and @U stand for the answers
-- Yes, No and "I am not sure" (the last becomes NOTHING).  Days are counted after an anchor date that is
-- itself day 0.  A case that expects NOTHING is a case outside the encoding: the Regulations do not answer it.

§ `Cases -- the relevant person and its compliance officer`

§§ `Being asked for information, and inspected (regulations 65 to 74)`

#ASSERT `Under regulation 65(3), am I a connected person of a relevant person` `reg 65-110 Yes` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a director of a client company, a connected person under Schedule 5
#ASSERT `Under regulation 65(3), am I a connected person of a relevant person` `reg 65-110 No` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under regulation 65(3), am I a connected person of a relevant person` `reg 65-110 I am not sure` EQUALS NOTHING -- Schedule 5 has not answered: the seat does not guess

-- 66(1).  Inputs: the body is a supervisory authority; I am a relevant person; payment service provider; connected person; in writing; what the notice requires; time and place specified.
#ASSERT `Under regulation 66(1), may a supervisory authority require me to provide information or produce documents` `reg 65-110 Yes` `reg 65-110 Yes` FALSE `reg 65-110 No` TRUE `reg 66(1)(a) the notice requires P to provide specified information, or information of a specified description` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a bank is asked in writing to provide information
#ASSERT `Under regulation 66(1), may a supervisory authority require me to provide information or produce documents` `reg 65-110 Yes` `reg 65-110 Yes` FALSE `reg 65-110 No` TRUE `reg 66(1)(b) the notice requires P to produce specified documents, or documents of a specified description` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- to produce documents
#ASSERT `Under regulation 66(1), may a supervisory authority require me to provide information or produce documents` `reg 65-110 Yes` `reg 65-110 Yes` FALSE `reg 65-110 No` TRUE `reg 66(1)(c) the notice requires P to attend before an officer at a time and place specified in the notice and answer questions` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- to attend at a stated time and place
#ASSERT `Under regulation 66(1), may a supervisory authority require me to provide information or produce documents` `reg 65-110 Yes` `reg 65-110 Yes` FALSE `reg 65-110 No` TRUE `reg 66(1)(c) the notice requires P to attend before an officer at a time and place specified in the notice and answer questions` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- attendance without a stated time and place
#ASSERT `Under regulation 66(1), may a supervisory authority require me to provide information or produce documents` `reg 65-110 Yes` `reg 65-110 Yes` FALSE `reg 65-110 No` FALSE `reg 66(1)(a) the notice requires P to provide specified information, or information of a specified description` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- the notice is not in writing
#ASSERT `Under regulation 66(1), may a supervisory authority require me to provide information or produce documents` `reg 65-110 Yes` `reg 65-110 No` TRUE `reg 65-110 No` TRUE `reg 66(1)(a) the notice requires P to provide specified information, or information of a specified description` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a payment service provider
#ASSERT `Under regulation 66(1), may a supervisory authority require me to provide information or produce documents` `reg 65-110 I am not sure` `reg 65-110 Yes` FALSE `reg 65-110 No` TRUE `reg 66(1)(a) the notice requires P to provide specified information, or information of a specified description` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not sure the body is a supervisory authority

#ASSERT `Under regulation 66(1A), does the power include requiring a copy of a suspicious activity report` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a copy of a suspicious activity disclosure to the NCA
#ASSERT `Under regulation 66(1A), does the power include requiring a copy of a suspicious activity report` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- the list is not closed

-- 66(2)(a).  Inputs: the period specified (-1 if none); reasonable; the day provided.
#ASSERT `Under regulation 66(2)(a), did I provide the information or documents in time` 14 TRUE 10 EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a 14-day period, provided on day 10
#ASSERT `Under regulation 66(2)(a), did I provide the information or documents in time` 14 TRUE 14 EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the last day of the period
#ASSERT `Under regulation 66(2)(a), did I provide the information or documents in time` 14 TRUE 15 EQUALS JUST FALSE -- one day late
#ASSERT `Under regulation 66(2)(a), did I provide the information or documents in time` 14 FALSE 15 EQUALS NOTHING -- an unreasonable period is not "such reasonable period"
#ASSERT `Under regulation 66(2)(a), did I provide the information or documents in time` (0 - 1) TRUE 3 EQUALS NOTHING -- no period was specified

#ASSERT `Under regulation 66(2)(b), did I provide the information or documents at the specified place` `reg 65-110 Yes` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under regulation 66(2)(b), did I provide the information or documents at the specified place` `reg 65-110 No` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under regulation 66(2)(b), did I provide the information or documents at the specified place` `reg 65-110 I am not sure` EQUALS NOTHING -- no place was specified

#ASSERT `Under regulation 66(3), may an officer require me to provide information or produce documents` `reg 65-110 Yes` TRUE `reg 65-110 Yes` `reg 66(3)(a) the officer requires P to provide specified information, or information of a specified description` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- an officer with written authorisation asks for information
#ASSERT `Under regulation 66(3), may an officer require me to provide information or produce documents` `reg 65-110 Yes` TRUE `reg 65-110 Yes` `reg 66(3) the officer requires something else of P` EQUALS NOTHING -- the list is not closed
#ASSERT `Under regulation 66(3), may an officer require me to provide information or produce documents` `reg 65-110 Yes` FALSE `reg 65-110 Yes` `reg 66(3)(a) the officer requires P to provide specified information, or information of a specified description` EQUALS JUST FALSE -- no authorisation in writing: reg 66(4) "may only be exercised ... by an officer authorised" (marginal reading (a); was NOTHING)
#ASSERT `Under regulation 66(3), may an officer require me to provide information or produce documents` `reg 65-110 Yes` TRUE `reg 65-110 No` `reg 66(3)(a) the officer requires P to provide specified information, or information of a specified description` EQUALS JUST FALSE -- not reasonably required in connection with supervisory functions (reg 66(4))
#ASSERT `Under regulation 66(3), may an officer require me to provide information or produce documents` `reg 65-110 No` TRUE `reg 65-110 Yes` `reg 66(3)(a) the officer requires P to provide specified information, or information of a specified description` EQUALS NOTHING -- not an officer: who may ask is a scope limit (ruled 2026-11-05, (c))

-- 66(5).  Inputs: what the notice requires; the notice sets out the reasons; the authority is not permitted to disclose them.
#ASSERT `Under regulation 66(5), does the notice I received set out the reasons it must` `reg 66(1)(a) the notice requires P to provide specified information, or information of a specified description` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under regulation 66(5), does the notice I received set out the reasons it must` `reg 66(1)(b) the notice requires P to produce specified documents, or documents of a specified description` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- no reasons, and no bar on disclosing them
#ASSERT `Under regulation 66(5), does the notice I received set out the reasons it must` `reg 66(1)(b) the notice requires P to produce specified documents, or documents of a specified description` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "unless the supervisory authority ... is not permitted to disclose"
#ASSERT `Under regulation 66(5), does the notice I received set out the reasons it must` `reg 66(1)(c) the notice requires P to attend before an officer at a time and place specified in the notice and answer questions` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- the paragraph speaks of information and documents, not attendance

#ASSERT `Under regulation 66(7), does producing the document affect a lien on it` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "does not affect any lien"
#ASSERT `Under regulation 66(7), does producing the document affect a lien on it` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `Under regulation 66(8), may the supervisory authority use the power against a third person who holds my document` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under regulation 66(8), may the supervisory authority use the power against a third person who holds my document` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the document does not appear to be with a third person: a failed "if" (marginal reading (a); was NOTHING)

-- 69(1).  Inputs: a duly authorised officer; of or acting for a supervisory authority; I am a relevant person; payment service provider; grounds (two).
#ASSERT `Under regulation 69(1), may an officer use the powers of entry on my premises` `reg 65-110 Yes` TRUE `reg 65-110 Yes` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under regulation 69(1), may an officer use the powers of entry on my premises` `reg 65-110 Yes` TRUE `reg 65-110 I am not sure` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a payment service provider
#ASSERT `Under regulation 69(1), may an officer use the powers of entry on my premises` `reg 65-110 I am not sure` TRUE `reg 65-110 Yes` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not sure the person is a duly authorised officer
#ASSERT `Under regulation 69(1), may an officer use the powers of entry on my premises` `reg 65-110 Yes` FALSE `reg 65-110 Yes` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- not an officer of or acting for a supervisory authority (ruled 2026-11-05; was NOTHING)
#ASSERT `Under regulation 69(1), may an officer use the powers of entry on my premises` `reg 65-110 Yes` TRUE `reg 65-110 Yes` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- no reasonable grounds to believe P may have contravened the requirements: "applies where" (ruled 2026-11-05 (b); was NOTHING)
#ASSERT `Under regulation 69(1), may an officer use the powers of entry on my premises` `reg 65-110 Yes` TRUE `reg 65-110 No` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- neither a relevant person nor a payment service provider (ruled 2026-11-05 (b); was NOTHING)

#ASSERT `Under regulation 69(2), may an officer enter my premises and exercise a power there` `reg 65-110 Yes` TRUE TRUE `reg 69(2)(a) enter the premises` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- enter the premises
#ASSERT `Under regulation 69(2), may an officer enter my premises and exercise a power there` `reg 65-110 Yes` TRUE TRUE `reg 69(2) some other power` EQUALS NOTHING -- the list is not closed
#ASSERT `Under regulation 69(2), may an officer enter my premises and exercise a power there` `reg 65-110 Yes` FALSE TRUE `reg 69(2)(a) enter the premises` EQUALS NOTHING -- no evidence of authority produced
#ASSERT `Under regulation 69(2), may an officer enter my premises and exercise a power there` `reg 65-110 Yes` TRUE FALSE `reg 69(2)(a) enter the premises` EQUALS NOTHING -- not at a reasonable time
#ASSERT `Under regulation 69(2), may an officer enter my premises and exercise a power there` `reg 65-110 No` TRUE TRUE `reg 69(2)(a) enter the premises` EQUALS JUST FALSE -- paragraph (2) does not apply: "Paragraph (2) applies where" (ruled 2026-11-05 (b); was NOTHING)

#ASSERT `Under regulation 69(3), may the officer take copies of, or make extracts from, my documents` `reg 65-110 Yes` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under regulation 69(3), may the officer take copies of, or make extracts from, my documents` `reg 65-110 Yes` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under regulation 69(3), may the officer take copies of, or make extracts from, my documents` `reg 65-110 No` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- paragraph (2) does not apply (ruled 2026-11-05 (b))

#ASSERT `Under regulation 71(1), may the seized material be retained` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under regulation 71(1), may the seized material be retained` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- no longer necessary to retain it rather than copies
#ASSERT `Under regulation 71(1), may the seized material be retained` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not taken under regulation 66 or 70

#ASSERT `Under regulation 71(3), may I apply for delivery of the material seized from me, and to which court` TRUE `England and Wales` EQUALS JUST `reg 71(3) the Crown Court`
#ASSERT `Under regulation 71(3), may I apply for delivery of the material seized from me, and to which court` TRUE `Scotland` EQUALS JUST `reg 71(3) the sheriff or the summary sheriff`
#ASSERT `Under regulation 71(3), may I apply for delivery of the material seized from me, and to which court` FALSE `Scotland` EQUALS NOTHING -- not the owner

-- 72(1).  Inputs: made under regulation 66, 69, 70, 74A or 74B; to produce excluded material; privileged; a lawyer; the full name and address of a client.
#ASSERT `Under regulation 72(1), may I be required to produce this material or give this information` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "may not be required ... to produce excluded material"
#ASSERT `Under regulation 72(1), may I be required to produce this material or give this information` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- legal professional privilege
#ASSERT `Under regulation 72(1), may I be required to produce this material or give this information` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a lawyer may be required to give the client's full name and address

#ASSERT `Under regulation 72(3), does civil liability arise because I made the disclosure` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- good faith, in accordance with the Regulations
#ASSERT `Under regulation 72(3), does civil liability arise because I made the disclosure` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not in good faith

#ASSERT `Under regulation 72(5), is the material privileged material` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under regulation 72(5), is the material privileged material` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

#ASSERT `Under regulation 72(7), is the material excluded material` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- personal records held in confidence
#ASSERT `Under regulation 72(7), is the material excluded material` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under regulation 72(7), is the material excluded material` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- not personal records

#ASSERT `Under regulation 73, is my statement protected from use in evidence against me in criminal proceedings` TRUE `reg 73(2) none of these cases` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a statement made in response to a requirement is protected
#ASSERT `Under regulation 73, is my statement protected from use in evidence against me in criminal proceedings` TRUE `reg 73(2)(e) a prosecution for an offence under regulation 88` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- a prosecution for an offence under regulation 88
#ASSERT `Under regulation 73, is my statement protected from use in evidence against me in criminal proceedings` TRUE `reg 73(2)(f) some other offence where, in giving evidence, the person makes a statement inconsistent with the statement mentioned in paragraph (1)` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (f) without the paragraph (3) trigger
#ASSERT `Under regulation 73, is my statement protected from use in evidence against me in criminal proceedings` TRUE `reg 73(2)(f) some other offence where, in giving evidence, the person makes a statement inconsistent with the statement mentioned in paragraph (1)` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- (f) with the paragraph (3) trigger

-- 74A(1).  Inputs: the kind of relevant person; the FCA directed; about compliance; required for a purpose; otherwise reasonably required.
