§ `Schedule 4 -- the information my supervisory authority is asked for (lines 3206-3241)`

-- Under schedule 4 item 1, am I a supervised person whom my supervisory authority counts
-- supervised directly
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 4 item 1, am I a supervised person whom my supervisory authority counts` WITH `I am subject to the supervision of my supervisory authority` IS TRUE, `my supervisory authority is a self-regulatory organisation` IS FALSE, `I am a member of that self-regulatory organisation` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a member of the self-regulatory organisation
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 4 item 1, am I a supervised person whom my supervisory authority counts` WITH `I am subject to the supervision of my supervisory authority` IS FALSE, `my supervisory authority is a self-regulatory organisation` IS TRUE, `I am a member of that self-regulatory organisation` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not supervised and not a member: the text does not say you are not a supervised person
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 4 item 1, am I a supervised person whom my supervisory authority counts` WITH `I am subject to the supervision of my supervisory authority` IS FALSE, `my supervisory authority is a self-regulatory organisation` IS FALSE, `I am a member of that self-regulatory organisation` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Under schedule 4, is my supervisory authority asked for an item of the supervisory information
-- item 5, the services provided by supervised persons: asked of every authority
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 4, is my supervisory authority asked for an item of the supervisory information` WITH `the position of the item in the printed order` IS 5, `my supervisory authority is a self-regulatory organisation` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- item 3 begins 'In the case of a self-regulatory organisation': asked of one
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 4, is my supervisory authority asked for an item of the supervisory information` WITH `the position of the item in the printed order` IS 3, `my supervisory authority is a self-regulatory organisation` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- item 3 and an authority that is not one: the item says nothing of it
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 4, is my supervisory authority asked for an item of the supervisory information` WITH `the position of the item in the printed order` IS 3, `my supervisory authority is a self-regulatory organisation` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- there is no item 22
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 4, is my supervisory authority asked for an item of the supervisory information` WITH `the position of the item in the printed order` IS 22, `my supervisory authority is a self-regulatory organisation` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Under schedule 4 item 17, is my supervisory authority asked for a copy of a suspicious activity disclosure that I have made to the NCA
-- any supervisory authority
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 4 item 17, is my supervisory authority asked for a copy of a suspicious activity disclosure that I have made to the NCA` WITH `my supervisory authority is a self-regulatory organisation` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a self-regulatory organisation
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 4 item 17, is my supervisory authority asked for a copy of a suspicious activity disclosure that I have made to the NCA` WITH `my supervisory authority is a self-regulatory organisation` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Under schedule 4 item 6, under which limb is a firm counted that my supervisory authority considers to be at a given level of risk
-- high risk is limb (a)
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 4 item 6, under which limb is a firm counted that my supervisory authority considers to be at a given level of risk` WITH `the level of risk at which the authority rates the firm` IS `sch 4 high risk`) EQUALS "(a)"
-- medium risk is limb (b)
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 4 item 6, under which limb is a firm counted that my supervisory authority considers to be at a given level of risk` WITH `the level of risk at which the authority rates the firm` IS `sch 4 medium risk`) EQUALS "(b)"
-- low risk is limb (c)
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 4 item 6, under which limb is a firm counted that my supervisory authority considers to be at a given level of risk` WITH `the level of risk at which the authority rates the firm` IS `sch 4 low risk`) EQUALS "(c)"

§ `Schedule 5 -- who is a connected person of my business (lines 3242-3255)`

-- Under schedule 5, is this person a connected person of my business
-- paragraph 1(a): an officer of a company
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 5, is this person a connected person of my business` WITH `the legal form of my business` IS `a company`, `the person is, or has been, an officer of my business` IS TRUE, `the person is, or has been, a manager of my business` IS FALSE, `the person is, or has been, an officer of a parent undertaking of my business` IS FALSE, `the person is, or has been, a manager of a parent undertaking of my business` IS FALSE, `the person is, or has been, an employee of my business` IS FALSE, `the person is, or has been, an agent of my business` IS FALSE, `the person is, or has been, an agent of a parent undertaking of my business` IS FALSE, `the person is, or has been, a member of my business` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- paragraph 1(b): an officer of a parent undertaking
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 5, is this person a connected person of my business` WITH `the legal form of my business` IS `a company`, `the person is, or has been, an officer of my business` IS FALSE, `the person is, or has been, a manager of my business` IS FALSE, `the person is, or has been, an officer of a parent undertaking of my business` IS TRUE, `the person is, or has been, a manager of a parent undertaking of my business` IS FALSE, `the person is, or has been, an employee of my business` IS FALSE, `the person is, or has been, an agent of my business` IS FALSE, `the person is, or has been, an agent of a parent undertaking of my business` IS FALSE, `the person is, or has been, a member of my business` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a company and a person with none of the listed roles: regulation 65(3) hands the definition to the Schedule's list, so the person is not a connected person (ruling of 2026-11-05)
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 5, is this person a connected person of my business` WITH `the legal form of my business` IS `a company`, `the person is, or has been, an officer of my business` IS FALSE, `the person is, or has been, a manager of my business` IS FALSE, `the person is, or has been, an officer of a parent undertaking of my business` IS FALSE, `the person is, or has been, a manager of a parent undertaking of my business` IS FALSE, `the person is, or has been, an employee of my business` IS FALSE, `the person is, or has been, an agent of my business` IS FALSE, `the person is, or has been, an agent of a parent undertaking of my business` IS FALSE, `the person is, or has been, a member of my business` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- paragraph 4: an employee of an individual
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 5, is this person a connected person of my business` WITH `the legal form of my business` IS `an individual`, `the person is, or has been, an officer of my business` IS FALSE, `the person is, or has been, a manager of my business` IS FALSE, `the person is, or has been, an officer of a parent undertaking of my business` IS FALSE, `the person is, or has been, a manager of a parent undertaking of my business` IS FALSE, `the person is, or has been, an employee of my business` IS TRUE, `the person is, or has been, an agent of my business` IS FALSE, `the person is, or has been, an agent of a parent undertaking of my business` IS FALSE, `the person is, or has been, a member of my business` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- paragraph 2: a member of a partnership
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 5, is this person a connected person of my business` WITH `the legal form of my business` IS `a partnership other than a limited liability partnership`, `the person is, or has been, an officer of my business` IS FALSE, `the person is, or has been, a manager of my business` IS FALSE, `the person is, or has been, an officer of a parent undertaking of my business` IS FALSE, `the person is, or has been, a manager of a parent undertaking of my business` IS FALSE, `the person is, or has been, an employee of my business` IS FALSE, `the person is, or has been, an agent of my business` IS FALSE, `the person is, or has been, an agent of a parent undertaking of my business` IS FALSE, `the person is, or has been, a member of my business` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a trust is none of the four forms the paragraphs name
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 5, is this person a connected person of my business` WITH `the legal form of my business` IS `a trust`, `the person is, or has been, an officer of my business` IS TRUE, `the person is, or has been, a manager of my business` IS FALSE, `the person is, or has been, an officer of a parent undertaking of my business` IS FALSE, `the person is, or has been, a manager of a parent undertaking of my business` IS FALSE, `the person is, or has been, an employee of my business` IS FALSE, `the person is, or has been, an agent of my business` IS FALSE, `the person is, or has been, an agent of a parent undertaking of my business` IS FALSE, `the person is, or has been, a member of my business` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- an officer of an individual: paragraph 4 lists employees and agents only, and regulation 65(3) hands the definition to that list, so an officer is not connected (ruling of 2026-11-05)
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 5, is this person a connected person of my business` WITH `the legal form of my business` IS `an individual`, `the person is, or has been, an officer of my business` IS TRUE, `the person is, or has been, a manager of my business` IS FALSE, `the person is, or has been, an officer of a parent undertaking of my business` IS FALSE, `the person is, or has been, a manager of a parent undertaking of my business` IS FALSE, `the person is, or has been, an employee of my business` IS FALSE, `the person is, or has been, an agent of my business` IS FALSE, `the person is, or has been, an agent of a parent undertaking of my business` IS FALSE, `the person is, or has been, a member of my business` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Schedule 6 -- is a requirement a relevant requirement (lines 3256-3348)`

-- Under schedule 6, is this requirement a relevant requirement
-- Article 4 of the funds transfer regulation, imposed on a payer's payment service provider
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 6, is this requirement a relevant requirement` WITH `the instrument the requirement is in` IS `sch 6 the funds transfer regulation`, `the number of the Article or regulation as printed` IS "4", `the paragraph of it as printed, or empty if you mean the whole` IS "", `on whom the requirement is imposed` IS `sch 6 the payment service provider of a payer`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- regulation 28(11), customer due diligence, imposed on a relevant person
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 6, is this requirement a relevant requirement` WITH `the instrument the requirement is in` IS `sch 6 these Regulations`, `the number of the Article or regulation as printed` IS "28", `the paragraph of it as printed, or empty if you mean the whole` IS "11", `on whom the requirement is imposed` IS `sch 6 any other person`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- regulation 26 as a whole: the list covers only some of its paragraphs
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 6, is this requirement a relevant requirement` WITH `the instrument the requirement is in` IS `sch 6 these Regulations`, `the number of the Article or regulation as printed` IS "26", `the paragraph of it as printed, or empty if you mean the whole` IS "", `on whom the requirement is imposed` IS `sch 6 any other person`) EQUALS NOTHING
-- regulation 22, which no list names
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 6, is this requirement a relevant requirement` WITH `the instrument the requirement is in` IS `sch 6 these Regulations`, `the number of the Article or regulation as printed` IS "22", `the paragraph of it as printed, or empty if you mean the whole` IS "", `on whom the requirement is imposed` IS `sch 6 any other person`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- regulation 28 imposed on an auction platform: limb (b) leaves out requirements on auction platforms, and limb (c) does not name it
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 6, is this requirement a relevant requirement` WITH `the instrument the requirement is in` IS `sch 6 these Regulations`, `the number of the Article or regulation as printed` IS "28", `the paragraph of it as printed, or empty if you mean the whole` IS "", `on whom the requirement is imposed` IS `sch 6 an auction platform`) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Schedule 6A -- the NCA and the financial intelligence unit (lines 3349-3390)`

-- Under schedule 6A paragraph 5(a), may the NCA use its powers to seek an order from me for information
-- all three conditions
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 6A paragraph 5(a), may the NCA use its powers to seek an order from me for information` WITH `a foreign financial intelligence unit has made a request to the NCA` IS TRUE, `the NCA has no information that it considers relevant to the request` IS TRUE, `the NCA suspects that I hold such information` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the NCA does not suspect that you hold the information: the paragraph's "Where" is not met, so the permission does not arise
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 6A paragraph 5(a), may the NCA use its powers to seek an order from me for information` WITH `a foreign financial intelligence unit has made a request to the NCA` IS TRUE, `the NCA has no information that it considers relevant to the request` IS TRUE, `the NCA suspects that I hold such information` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Under schedule 6A paragraph 14, must the NCA address a request for information about me to the foreign financial intelligence unit of the state of my head office
-- a business headquartered in another EEA state that the NCA wants information about
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 6A paragraph 14, must the NCA address a request for information about me to the foreign financial intelligence unit of the state of my head office` WITH `the NCA wishes to obtain information about my business` IS TRUE, `my business has its head office in an EEA state other than the United Kingdom` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a business headquartered in the United Kingdom: paragraph 13 says paragraphs 14 and 15 apply where the head office is in another EEA state, so they do not apply
