-- Under schedule 7 paragraph 3(2), must the ombudsman rules make a person we identified as politically exposed eligible to complain
-- identified as a politically exposed person and complaining of the identification
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 7 paragraph 3(2), must the ombudsman rules make a person we identified as politically exposed eligible to complain` WITH `the person has been identified by the respondent, in carrying on an activity to which the rules apply, as a politically exposed person` IS TRUE, `the person has been identified by the respondent, in carrying on an activity to which the rules apply, as a family member of a politically exposed person` IS FALSE, `the person has been identified by the respondent, in carrying on an activity to which the rules apply, as a known close associate of a politically exposed person` IS FALSE, `the complainant complains that the complainant has been incorrectly identified as a person within subsection (7B)` IS TRUE, `the complaint relates to an act or omission of the respondent in consequence of the identification of the complainant as a person within subsection (7B)` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- identified as a known close associate and complaining of what followed
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 7 paragraph 3(2), must the ombudsman rules make a person we identified as politically exposed eligible to complain` WITH `the person has been identified by the respondent, in carrying on an activity to which the rules apply, as a politically exposed person` IS FALSE, `the person has been identified by the respondent, in carrying on an activity to which the rules apply, as a family member of a politically exposed person` IS FALSE, `the person has been identified by the respondent, in carrying on an activity to which the rules apply, as a known close associate of a politically exposed person` IS TRUE, `the complainant complains that the complainant has been incorrectly identified as a person within subsection (7B)` IS FALSE, `the complaint relates to an act or omission of the respondent in consequence of the identification of the complainant as a person within subsection (7B)` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not identified in any of the three ways
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 7 paragraph 3(2), must the ombudsman rules make a person we identified as politically exposed eligible to complain` WITH `the person has been identified by the respondent, in carrying on an activity to which the rules apply, as a politically exposed person` IS FALSE, `the person has been identified by the respondent, in carrying on an activity to which the rules apply, as a family member of a politically exposed person` IS FALSE, `the person has been identified by the respondent, in carrying on an activity to which the rules apply, as a known close associate of a politically exposed person` IS FALSE, `the complainant complains that the complainant has been incorrectly identified as a person within subsection (7B)` IS TRUE, `the complaint relates to an act or omission of the respondent in consequence of the identification of the complainant as a person within subsection (7B)` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- identified, but complaining of something else
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 7 paragraph 3(2), must the ombudsman rules make a person we identified as politically exposed eligible to complain` WITH `the person has been identified by the respondent, in carrying on an activity to which the rules apply, as a politically exposed person` IS TRUE, `the person has been identified by the respondent, in carrying on an activity to which the rules apply, as a family member of a politically exposed person` IS FALSE, `the person has been identified by the respondent, in carrying on an activity to which the rules apply, as a known close associate of a politically exposed person` IS FALSE, `the complainant complains that the complainant has been incorrectly identified as a person within subsection (7B)` IS FALSE, `the complaint relates to an act or omission of the respondent in consequence of the identification of the complainant as a person within subsection (7B)` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Under schedule 7 paragraph 12, does paragraph 2 of Schedule 3 to the Estate Agents Order 1991 apply to me when I could not complete customer due diligence
-- unable to apply regulation 28's measures
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 7 paragraph 12, does paragraph 2 of Schedule 3 to the Estate Agents Order 1991 apply to me when I could not complete customer due diligence` WITH `the estate agent does not forward accurate details of the offer` IS TRUE, `the estate agent is unable to apply the customer due diligence measures required by regulation 28` IS TRUE, `regulations 33 and 35 to 37 are relevant in relation to the offeror` IS FALSE, `the estate agent is unable to apply the customer due diligence measures required by regulations 33 and 35 to 37 in relation to the offeror` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- able to apply every measure required
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 7 paragraph 12, does paragraph 2 of Schedule 3 to the Estate Agents Order 1991 apply to me when I could not complete customer due diligence` WITH `the estate agent does not forward accurate details of the offer` IS TRUE, `the estate agent is unable to apply the customer due diligence measures required by regulation 28` IS FALSE, `regulations 33 and 35 to 37 are relevant in relation to the offeror` IS TRUE, `the estate agent is unable to apply the customer due diligence measures required by regulations 33 and 35 to 37 in relation to the offeror` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- you did forward accurate details
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 7 paragraph 12, does paragraph 2 of Schedule 3 to the Estate Agents Order 1991 apply to me when I could not complete customer due diligence` WITH `the estate agent does not forward accurate details of the offer` IS FALSE, `the estate agent is unable to apply the customer due diligence measures required by regulation 28` IS TRUE, `regulations 33 and 35 to 37 are relevant in relation to the offeror` IS FALSE, `the estate agent is unable to apply the customer due diligence measures required by regulations 33 and 35 to 37 in relation to the offeror` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Under schedule 7 paragraph 18, may my open-ended investment company issue bearer shares
-- authorised in 2020, applied and determined in 2020
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 7 paragraph 18, may my open-ended investment company issue bearer shares` WITH `the date on which the open-ended investment company was authorised` IS (Date 1 2 2020), `the date on which an application for an authorisation order was made in relation to the company` IS (Date 1 1 2020), `the date on which that application was determined` IS (Date 1 2 2020)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- authorised on 26 June 2017, the day the Regulations came into force
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 7 paragraph 18, may my open-ended investment company issue bearer shares` WITH `the date on which the open-ended investment company was authorised` IS (Date 26 6 2017), `the date on which an application for an authorisation order was made in relation to the company` IS (Date 1 5 2017), `the date on which that application was determined` IS (Date 1 5 2017)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- authorised on 25 June 2017: regulation 48(1) governs it and is not among the sources
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 7 paragraph 18, may my open-ended investment company issue bearer shares` WITH `the date on which the open-ended investment company was authorised` IS (Date 25 6 2017), `the date on which an application for an authorisation order was made in relation to the company` IS (Date 1 5 2017), `the date on which that application was determined` IS (Date 1 5 2017)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- authorised on 1 August 2017 after an application made in June and determined on that day: paragraph (3) lifts paragraph (2)
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 7 paragraph 18, may my open-ended investment company issue bearer shares` WITH `the date on which the open-ended investment company was authorised` IS (Date 1 8 2017), `the date on which an application for an authorisation order was made in relation to the company` IS (Date 1 6 2017), `the date on which that application was determined` IS (Date 1 8 2017)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Under schedule 7 paragraph 18, is a provision in my open-ended investment company's instrument of incorporation authorising bearer shares void
-- authorised in 2020 with such a provision
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 7 paragraph 18, is a provision in my open-ended investment company's instrument of incorporation authorising bearer shares void` WITH `a provision in the instrument of incorporation purports to authorise the company to issue bearer shares` IS TRUE, `the date on which the open-ended investment company was authorised` IS (Date 1 2 2020), `the date on which an application for an authorisation order was made in relation to the company` IS (Date 1 1 2020), `the date on which that application was determined` IS (Date 1 2 2020)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no such provision
#ASSERT (`Under schedule 7 paragraph 18, is a provision in my open-ended investment company's instrument of incorporation authorising bearer shares void` WITH `a provision in the instrument of incorporation purports to authorise the company to issue bearer shares` IS FALSE, `the date on which the open-ended investment company was authorised` IS (Date 1 2 2020), `the date on which an application for an authorisation order was made in relation to the company` IS (Date 1 1 2020), `the date on which that application was determined` IS (Date 1 2 2020)) EQUALS NOTHING
